  "name": "Sindhen melismatic voice",
  "desc": "A Javanese sindhen-style pitched vocal: a pitchable diphone tracing melismatic pentatonic phrases with quick ornamental turns and grace-note bends over a Db major pentatonic. Sparse breathes one spacious descending melisma per phrase; full ornaments densely with a semitone grace-echo and a saw pump; peak cascades three-note turns, an octave shimmer halo and a phrase-end bend down. Expressive, ceremonial, floating. scale-sub transposable.",
